          %meta{:content => "application/xhtml+xml;charset=utf-8", "http-equiv" => "Content-type"}/
          %title
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.nikhef.nl/~t58/Site/Home.html"} personal page
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/authors/1022935"} inSpire page
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/authors/1022935"} GoogleScholar page
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/search/?searchtype=author&query=Schellekens%2C+A"} arXiv page
          %p
            Bert Schellekens has been working on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            and specifically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SCFT"} SCFT
            in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+building"} model building
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+conformal+field+theory"} RCFT
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+model"} Gepner model
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactifications
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            (via
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+states"} boundary states
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
          %p
            Recognizing the abundance of semi-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} realistic models
            (
            %a{:href => "#LercheLustSchellekens86"}> Lerche-Lüst-Schellekens 86
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#LercheLustSchellekens87"} Lerche-Lüst-Schellekens 87
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of string theory vacua
            and to coin that term in the first place (
            %a{:href => "#Schellekens98"}> Schellekens 98
            , see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schellekens06"} Schellekens 06
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schellekens08"} Schellekens 08
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schellekens16"} Schellekens 16
          %p
            Schellekens’ scans of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"}> landscape
            ” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+algebra"} vertex-algebraically
            well-defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+model"} Gepner model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            (in the sense of
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.physicsforums.com/insights/spectral-standard-model-string-compactifications/"} Spectral Standard Models and String Compactifications
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            (via
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+states"} boundary states
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            (
            %a{:href => "#DijkstraHuiszoonSchellekens04a"}> Dijkstra-Huiszoon-Schellekens 04a
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#DijkstraHuiszoonSchellekens04b"} Dijkstra-Huiszoon-Schellekens 04b
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of string theory vacua
            is possible, worthwhile and probably necessary.
          %p
            As an example, from
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DijkstraHuiszoonSchellekens04b"} Dijkstra-Huiszoon-Schellekens 04b
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constants"} coupling constants
            in a computer scan of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+model"} Gepner model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
            theory. The faint lines are NOT drawn by hand, but reflect increased density of Gepner models as seen by the computer scan.
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SchellekensSuperGepnerModelScanII.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lerche"}> Wolfgang Lerche
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+L%C3%BCst"} Dieter Lüst
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adrian+Norbert+Schellekens"} Adrian Norbert Schellekens
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Ten-dimensional heterotic strings from Niemeier lattices
                %strong 181
                1–2 (1986) 71-75 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(86)91257-8"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(86)91257-8
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/233203"} inspire:233203
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (relation to
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niemeier+lattices"} Niemeier lattices
            %li#LercheLustSchellekens87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lerche"}> Wolfgang Lerche
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+L%C3%BCst"} Dieter Lüst
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Schellekens"} Bert Schellekens
                %em Chiral Four-dimensional Heterotic Strings from Self-dual Lattices
                Nucl. Phys. B 287, 477, 1987 (
                %a{:href => "http://lerche.web.cern.ch/lerche/papers/4dhetstrings.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Schellekens91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Schellekens"}> Bert Schellekens
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classification of Ten-Dimensional Heterotic Strings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9112006"} arXiv:hep-th/9112006
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+form"} modular form
            with values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strengths"} field strengths
            (“character-valued partition function”, a little later called the
            = succeed "/" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly+cancellation"} Green-Schwarz anomaly cancellation
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+N.+Schellekens"}> A. N. Schellekens
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+P.+Warner"} Nicholas P. Warner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anomalies, characters and strings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(87)90108-8"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(87)90108-8
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+N.+Schellekens"}> A. N. Schellekens
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+P.+Warner"} Nicholas P. Warner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anomalies and modular invariance in string theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(86)90760-4"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(86)90760-4
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lerche"}> Wolfgang Lerche
